{
  "$comment": [
    "The allowlisted source registry (M24). Data, not code: adding a source is a",
    "review of this file, not a deploy of new logic.",
    "",
    "Three deliberate properties of this list:",
    "",
    "1. It includes many outlets that carry the same wire services (PTI, ANI).",
    "   That is the point. Origin clustering has to have real duplicates to collapse,",
    "   and the M26 gate requires at least one multi-outlet cluster in the live",
    "   corpus. Subscribing to outlets that reprint the same wire is a feed-selection",
    "   decision, not synthetic data.",
    "",
    "   'carries_wire' marks the outlets added for that reason: regional papers and",
    "   aggregators that republish agency copy substantially unedited. National",
    "   mastheads were measured writing their own copy (cross-outlet Jaccard 0.00 to",
    "   0.04), so a list of only those cannot satisfy the gate however long it runs.",
    "   Measured in docs/ops-notes.md.",
    "",
    "2. Fact-checkers are marked source_class 'factchecker' and are the only sources",
    "   whose output can become Tier C evidence. News outlets are corroboration",
    "   material; they are not adjudications.",
    "",
    "3. Every URL here was fetched and parsed on 2026-08-16 and returned at least one",
    "   item. Thirteen of the previous thirty were dead — two of them fact-checkers,",
    "   which silently weakened the cheapest evidence class. Feeds are re-probed as",
    "   part of reviewing this file; a feed that cannot be verified is removed rather",
    "   than left in to fail quietly against backoff.",
    "",
    "4. The list is not Indian by rule — it is an allowlist, which is a fetch-security",
    "   and trust boundary, not a geography one. It is mostly Indian because the claim",
    "   distribution is. Non-Indian sources are included where they do specific work:",
    "",
    "   - International fact-checkers (Snopes, Full Fact) adjudicate claims that",
    "     circulate in India too, and their output is Tier C like any other.",
    "   - International desks covering foreign events are what date recycled foreign",
    "     imagery, which is among the largest categories of Indian visual",
    "     misinformation — a Syrian or Gaza photograph recaptioned as Kashmir needs",
    "     the original coverage to exist in the corpus before M33/M34 can find it.",
    "",
    "   Reuters, AP and AFP are deliberately absent: their public RSS endpoints are",
    "   retired (404/401/403 as of 2026-08-16) and their wire content is now sold",
    "   through paid APIs. Their copy still reaches the corpus second-hand through the",
    "   Indian outlets that carry it.",
    "",
    "'allowed_for_primary_check' marks domains whose own pages can settle an",
    "attribution question. It is false by default and set only for bodies that",
    "publish primary records."
  ],
